WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.525
 

00:00:00.525 --> 00:00:03.095
In this video you're going to learn how to navigate

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.540
the Algebra 1 final exam review

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:13.000
We're going to be going through together 33 different question types, in total, 80 different problems

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.340
So let's get started into this video. If you want to get the most out of it

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:15.975
I suggest

00:00:15.975 --> 00:00:18.925
Pausing the video, seeing if you can do the problem on your own

00:00:18.925 --> 00:00:21.935
And then we'll go through it together and  you can see which ones you need more help on

00:00:21.935 --> 00:00:24.905
And I've got videos going over these concepts in greater detail

00:00:24.905 --> 00:00:27.875
on my Mario's Math Tutoring YouTube channel

00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:30.875
so if you need help you can go there for additional resources

00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:33.695
Let's get started into the video the first question talks about

00:00:33.695 --> 00:00:36.685
solving an equation and this equation

00:00:36.685 --> 00:00:38.615
you can see is negative 3

00:00:39.395 --> 00:00:42.285
time x minus 2 minus 5 equals negative 11

00:00:42.295 --> 00:00:45.575
so what do you think, how would you solve that problem

00:00:45.575 --> 00:00:48.635
Well if I was going to solve it, what I would do is

00:00:48.635 --> 00:00:51.915
I would distribute this negative 3, okay, into the parentheses

00:00:51.915 --> 00:00:55.175
and that's going to give us negative 3x  and negative 3

00:00:55.175 --> 00:00:58.595
times a negative two give us positive 6, right

00:00:58.765 --> 00:01:01.985
minus 5, equals negative 11. I always like to combine

00:01:01.985 --> 00:01:03.505
like-terms first

00:01:04.045 --> 00:01:07.075
So that's going to be 6 minus 5, which is 1

00:01:07.075 --> 00:01:09.585
And then what we'll want to do

00:01:09.585 --> 00:01:12.505
is we want to get the variables on one side, numbers on the other

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.455
so we'll subtract 1 from both sides

00:01:15.455 --> 00:01:18.145
that gives us negative 3x equals negative 12

00:01:18.145 --> 00:01:21.635
and if I divide both sides by negative 3, you just want to get this x by itself

00:01:21.965 --> 00:01:24.915
you can see that we get x equals 4

00:01:24.915 --> 00:01:28.065
So the question that they were really testing you on in this particular problem

00:01:28.065 --> 00:01:31.125
is do you know the distributive property?

00:01:31.125 --> 00:01:32.625
And do you know how to solve

00:01:33.135 --> 00:01:36.195
equations? So that's how you do the first one, let's

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:37.195
go to the second one now,

00:01:37.755 --> 00:01:38.755
It says, solve

00:01:39.005 --> 00:01:42.025
5x minus 2 divided by 20 equals x divided by 5

00:01:42.025 --> 00:01:44.795
So what do you think, what would you do to solve that problem?

00:01:45.675 --> 00:01:48.665
Well, if I was going to do it, what I would do is I would

00:01:48.665 --> 00:01:51.885
use the cross-multiplying technique, okay

00:01:51.885 --> 00:01:54.855
so I would multiply on the diagonals. So 5x minus 2

00:01:54.855 --> 00:01:56.605
times 5, alright

00:01:58.035 --> 00:02:01.065
Equals 20 times x

00:02:01.065 --> 00:02:03.855
Okay, so are you with me so far?
So then what I would do is I would

00:02:03.855 --> 00:02:09.765
distribute this 5 into the parentheses, that's 25x minus 10, okay? Because 5 times negative 2 is negative 10

00:02:10.615 --> 00:02:13.555
And then what you want to do is you want to get the variables on one side and the numbers

00:02:13.555 --> 00:02:14.555
on the opposite side

00:02:14.875 --> 00:02:17.585
So what I'm going to do is I'm going to subtract

00:02:17.585 --> 00:02:20.255
the 25x from both sides.

00:02:20.255 --> 00:02:23.215
Now, a lot of students like to get the variables on the left, but it doesn't really matter

00:02:23.215 --> 00:02:25.875
as long as you get the numbers and the variables

00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:28.875
on opposite sides, that's the key. 20 minus 25

00:02:28.875 --> 00:02:31.965
is negative 5x. And then we just want to get the x by itself

00:02:31.965 --> 00:02:35.085
So the opposite of multiplying by negative 5

00:02:35.085 --> 00:02:38.115
would be to divide by negative 5. So negative

00:02:38.115 --> 00:02:41.115
10 divided by negative 5 is positive 2. These cancel

00:02:41.115 --> 00:02:43.735
You're just going to get x by itself and x equals 2

00:02:43.735 --> 00:02:46.705
Now, the nice thing about Algebra is that oftentimes you can check your answer

00:02:46.705 --> 00:02:49.535
by taking that value, 2, putting it into the original

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:52.565
problem wherever you see x, simplifying, and making sure that

00:02:52.565 --> 00:02:53.475
the left side and the right side

00:02:53.475 --> 00:02:55.995
equal each other. That way, you know you've got it right.

00:02:56.305 --> 00:02:59.305
Now, the question or the topic that you're tested on in this question

00:02:59.305 --> 00:03:02.195
is working with proportions. So proportions

00:03:02.195 --> 00:03:05.505
are a ratio equaled to a ratio. And you can use that cross multiplying technique

00:03:05.505 --> 00:03:06.615
or that cross product technique

00:03:07.295 --> 00:03:10.315
to solve the equation.

